# Core project conventions

- Prefer small, focused changes that match existing structure.
- All secrets and non-shareable env materials live under `.env/` (see `env-secrets` rule); never commit or bake them into images.
- Update `docs/requirements/` when a decision becomes a durable constraint (`write-requirements` skill).
- Update `.cursor/rules/` or `.cursor/skills/` when a convention should apply beyond one chat.
- Prefer unambiguous basenames and a single `run_checks` entrypoint (see always-apply rules).
- Do not add stack-specific scaffolding to the bootstrap template unless explicitly requested; see `docs/meta/COMMON-THREADS.md` before promoting a product skill here.
